2.43.0

Description: Fix CVE-2026-66011 — memory leak in InterpretImageProperties on
 malformed command-line arguments (CWE-401).
 .
 ImageMagick's command-line utilities (convert/mogrify/magick) route argument
 interpretation for options such as -set, -format, -annotate, -print and any
 "%[...]" percent-escape through MagickCore's InterpretImageProperties(). In
 the 6.9.x source shipped by Debian bookworm, several error/early-exit paths
 in that function (the interpret_text realloc macros, the "UnbalancedBraces"
 handler, and an unchecked AcquireFxInfo() path) either leaked the cloned
 ImageInfo (property_info) and/or the accumulating interpret_text buffer, or
 dereferenced a NULL FxInfo. Repeatedly supplying malformed arguments (e.g.
 an unbalanced "%[" or a failing "%[fx:...]") therefore leaks memory on each
 invocation, enabling resource/memory exhaustion.
 .
 This is a novel, adapted backport: the released upstream fix
 (e3e69118c29064e2716ca89aab635ea95a15dd49, ImageMagick 7.1.2-27,
 GHSA-cvhv-g4rq-3hmw) lives in the ImageMagick 7.x MagickWand/MagickCore
 tree (MagickWand/wandcli.c, magick-cli.c, operation.c, MagickCore/property.c)
 whose CLI-wand files do not exist in the 6.x codebase Debian ships. The
 portable, in-package root cause is the InterpretImageProperties() cleanup
 discipline, which this patch re-derives against magick/property.c: all
 error/early-exit paths now converge on a single "cleanup" label that always
 releases property_info and interpret_text, pointers are initialised to NULL,
 and AcquireFxInfo() is NULL-checked before use.
Origin: ai-synthesized, CVE-2026-66011
Bug: https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-cvhv-g4rq-3hmw
Author: Root.io Novel Patcher <security@root.io>
Last-Update: 2026-07-31
Forwarded: not-needed

--- a/magick/property.c
+++ b/magick/property.c
@@ -3632,9 +3632,8 @@
         MaxTextExtent,sizeof(*interpret_text)); \
       if (interpret_text == (char *) NULL) \
         { \
-          if (property_info != image_info) \
-            property_info=DestroyImageInfo(property_info); \
-          return((char *) NULL); \
+          status=MagickFalse; \
+          goto cleanup; \
         } \
       q=interpret_text+strlen(interpret_text); \
    } \
@@ -3650,9 +3649,8 @@
         MaxTextExtent,sizeof(*interpret_text)); \
